Robot: Inky  ROBOT_SSH=inky@inky  (network: tamu/tailscale)
Robot: Clyde  ROBOT_SSH=clyde@clyde  (network: tamu/tailscale)
Logs: /home/schen08/central-computer/entc641/data/runs/R12/fleet/20261119-141443-61723
Fleet bringup
  robots:       inky clyde
  filter:       -ic
  central host: reverie
  rviz:         off
  output:       warnings and errors
  ssh:
    inky -> inky@inky
    clyde -> clyde@clyde
Stages:
  1. ./scripts/comms/start_zenoh_central.sh -ic
     wait for each robot: Route Subscriber (Zenoh:<robot>/tf_zenoh -> ROS:/<robot>/tf_zenoh) created
  2. on each robot, in parallel:
       source scripts/env/ros_robot_env.bash
       export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger
       export LDS_MODEL=LDS-02
       ros2 launch turtlebot3_bringup robot.launch.py
     wait for: [<robot>.diff_drive_controller]: Run!
  3. on each robot, in parallel:
       ros2 launch turtlebot3_navigation2 navigation2_slam.launch.py
     wait for: [<robot>.startup_map_seeder]: Startup map seeding complete
  4. on each robot, in parallel:
       ./scripts/comms/start_zenoh_robot.sh reverie
     wait for: TF zenoh publish: /<robot>/tf -> /<robot>/tf_zenoh
     and both Nav2 action servers discovered (restarted once if not)
  5. ./scripts/core/start_central.sh -ic
     wait for: All services running.  Press Ctrl+C to stop.

